# Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# Auth is the owner's Claude subscription (Pro/Max): run `claude setup-token`
# once (1-year, inference-only OAuth token) and paste it here. The control
# plane injects it into run-bursts as the container's only Anthropic credential.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Fallback only — API billing. NOTE: if both are set, the runner injects the
# OAuth token and ignores this (the CLI itself would prefer the API key).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# GitHub App (the dev's scoped identity). The private key never leaves the
# control plane; each burst gets a fresh 1-hour installation token.
# App ID + key: the App's settings page. Installation ID: optional — discovered
# automatically when the App has exactly one installation.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
# GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=

# Machine review (REVIEWERS.md): a toggle and a selector, everything declared.
# REVIEW=on requires REVIEW_PROVIDERS to name at least one provider; a declaration
# that can't be honored (unknown name, missing credential) refuses to start.
# Providers: copilot (shipped) · claude, codex (REVIEWERS.md slices 2–3).
# REVIEW=off
# REVIEW_PROVIDERS=
# REVIEWER_MODEL=

# Credentials for the `claude` provider: a second GitHub App (the PR's author
# can't review it, so findings post under a distinct identity). Permissions:
# Pull requests read/write only, installed on the product repo. The reviewer
# burst itself gets NO GitHub credential — the control plane posts for it.
# REVIEWER_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# REVIEWER_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=

# Credential for the `copilot` provider: GitHub grants Copilot review requests
# only to a *user* token whose owner has a Copilot seat — an App/bot token gets
# HTTP 201 and the reviewer is silently dropped (verified 2026-07-03, PR #6).
# Fine-grained PAT of the owner: repository = the product repo, permission =
# Pull requests read/write. Used by the control plane for review requests only;
# never enters the burst container.
# GITHUB_COPILOT_REVIEW_TOKEN=

# E2E testing (TESTER.md): E2E=on runs a tester burst after a clean machine
# review, when the product ships a TESTING.md. Requires the claude review
# provider (the test stage triggers on its APPROVE).
E2E=off
# TESTER_MODEL=

# Sandbox credentials for tester bursts, under the TEST_ prefix — the allowlist
# boundary: only names the product's TESTING.md asks for AND that exist here
# are injected (as the unprefixed name), into tester bursts only. Provision
# disposable resources: for discord-bot, a dedicated test app + empty guild.
# TEST_DISCORD_TOKEN=
# TEST_GUILD_ID=

# Model policy: the model bursts run on. Precedence: --model flag > this var >
# the pinned platform default (control_plane.runner.DEFAULT_MODEL). The pin
# exists so "unset" never means "whatever `claude` in the image defaults to".
# DEV_AGENT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Scheduler rails (SCHEDULER.md) — hard limits on unattended behavior.
# Defaults shown; uncomment to override.
# SCHEDULER_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# SCHEDULER_MAX_REVIEW_ROUNDS=3
# SCHEDULER_DAILY_BURST_CEILING=20
# SCHEDULER_FAILURE_COOLDOWN_S=300
# SCHEDULER_POLL_INTERVAL_S=60
# SCHEDULER_BURST_BUDGET_USD=2.0   # HARD cap on estimated cost — the SDK kills the burst mid-run (resume makes retries continue, not restart)
# SCHEDULER_BURST_MAX_TURNS=100

# Tracing (ARCHITECTURE.md §9): set to export burst spans via OTLP. Port 4318 is
# an OTLP/HTTP collector's; a bare Phoenix listens on 6006 and takes traces only,
# which is why the dev rig puts a collector in front —
# `docker compose -f docker/compose.telemetry.yaml up -d --wait`, and
# OBSERVABILITY.md for the rest of the wiring.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# Where a *burst* pushes its own telemetry (B2) — Claude Code's traces and tool
# events, stamped with task/burst/role/kind. A separate variable from the one
# above because the container is in another network namespace: `localhost` inside
# the box is the box, and the CLI drops export failures silently. Unset ⇒ no
# telemetry env enters the container.
# DEV_AGENT_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:4318

# The two store toggles (STORES.md), independent of each other because a
# deployment can buy one capability before the other. Neither is a mode flag —
# each is the same design with and without a service behind it.
#
# The ledger: set it and the ledger is Postgres, whose schema
# `control-plane migrate` owns; unset, it is the single-node SQLite file under
# --data-dir, which needs no migration. The dev rig's DSN, connecting as the
# schema owner (docker/compose.yaml):
# LEDGER_DSN=postgresql://platform_admin:platform@localhost:5432/platform?sslmode=disable
#
# The session archive: set it and snapshots go to an S3 bucket; unset, they go to
# a directory under --data-dir, with the same keys. `tls=false` is this store's
# `sslmode=disable`; the bucket is created on first write if it doesn't exist.
# Credentials belong to the control plane alone — no burst ever holds them.
# ARCHIVE_URL=s3://platform:platform-dev-secret@localhost:8333/platform-sessions?tls=false
